  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#48516\"], \"answer\": \"This has been reported before in PowerToys#48516: since the per-monitor settings were added to the Command Palette Dock (0.100), the dock binds to specific monitors. When a monitor is disconnected and reconnected (as on laptops), the settings page lists only the built-in display, and the dock disappears, shows empty, or is scaled wrongly. That ticket has no confirmed fix or workaround in the thread. The expected behavior it asks for is for the dock to follow Windows' primary/non-primary monitor configuration, as it did in 0.99. For now, add your details and the 0.100.2 version to that ticket. Related reports of an empty dock on a secondary monitor are in PowerToys#49018, though that one doesn't involve reconnecting a monitor.\"}",
